      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Police appeal",
          "heading": "Two arrested after Hirwaun pub fight following Wales' win over All Blacks",
          "body": "South Wales Police are appealing for witnesses after a disturbance at the Glancynon Inn in Hirwaun, near Aberdare, at around 8.30pm on Saturday. Earlier that day, head coach Steve Tandy's side had beaten New Zealand 35-28 in Cardiff for a first win over the All Blacks since 1953. A fight is understood to have broken out inside the pub. Two people were arrested on suspicion of affray and have since been released on bail. Investigations are ongoing, and police have asked anyone who was inside the pub at the time to come forward."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
