          "kicker": "Coach's verdict",
          "heading": "Felipe Contepomi praises Pumas' character in Genoa win despite 13-man finish",
          "body": "Argentina head coach Felipe Contepomi conceded that Italy dominated possession and territory in the first half of Saturday's 19-14 win in Genoa, but said these matches are about converting chances and scoring. Above all he singled out his players' character, noting the side stayed connected through a fraught final 20 minutes, when yellow cards for Joel Sclavi and Efraín Elías left them with 13. He described a team still under construction, whose cohesion grows the longer it spends together, and noted the squad now has two weeks together."
        },
