          "heading": "Planet Rugby questions Les Kiss's authority after Wallabies' 15-12 Murrayfield defeat",
          "body": "Wallabies head coach Les Kiss is clearly useful as a specialist or assistant, a Planet Rugby column argues, but nothing in his post-match comments after Sunday's 15-12 Nations Championship loss to Scotland suggested the standing or authority to sell a vision to players or public. The piece also dismisses rugby league recruits as 'sugar-hits' — with Mark Nawaqanitawase returning to union and Angus Crichton set to follow his Sydney Roosters teammate — insisting Australia must develop forwards and a reliable first five-eighth."
