          "heading": "Sir Steve Hansen says Wales loss 'reminded' him of World Cup exits",
          "body": "Former All Blacks head coach Sir Steve Hansen told the Rugby Unity podcast that last weekend's 35-28 defeat to Wales came down to mindset: preparing well but subconsciously assuming victory means \"we wait for things to happen and there's no urgency\" until desperation sets in. He said the loss \"reminded\" him of the 2007 World Cup quarter-final defeat by France at the same Cardiff ground and the 19-7 semi-final defeat by England in 2019. He also felt the number of changes made by head coach Dave Rennie was a factor."
